x86_64-linux  there is nothing to compare here, by construction: a case that includes a C++ standard library header is compiled by clang against *clang's* library, not this one, so the two objects hold the symbols of two different implementations of std::forward and std::move. The forwarding shape itself - `_Z3setIRiEvOT_i` for an lvalue, T deduced as `U &` - is compared in reference-collapsing, which includes nothing; behaviour is the oracle here.
